      "writtenOn": "2022-08-22T01:15:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this looks like a flaw upstream to me.  the rebuilding of domains starts in a separate process caused by the notifier chain in cpufreq_online; the notifier in this case has been registered by arch_topology, for arm if I recall.  the notified function schedules work in a different process.\n\ncpufreq_online continues on and does a register_em, which initializes content that the rebuilding of domains is dependent on, the em_pd values.  if the separate process finishes building domains before cpufreq_online gets around to the register_em call, the root domains have their perf domain values wiped out.\n\nthis has nothing to do with our module.  we merely are the recipients of the bad rd-\u003epd data, which was bad well before the module gets loaded.",
      "parentUuid": "39f8fb5a_2da4498a",
      "revId": "eb610069f2ef107d84f1db0bf66ae090c7e258ba",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
